Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• ORDER_ITEMS."status": filter only the rows that correspond to completed sales (e.g. WHERE "status" = 'Complete').  
• ORDER_ITEMS."order_id": to count the number of distinct orders each month.  
• ORDER_ITEMS."product_id": join key that links an order line to a product.  
• ORDER_ITEMS."sale_price": to aggregate revenue.  
• ORDER_ITEMS."created_at": micro‑seconds epoch; will be converted to year‑month so we can group monthly.  

• PRODUCTS."id": primary key matching ORDER_ITEMS."product_id".  
• PRODUCTS."category": to segment orders / revenue by product category.  

Typical condition(s) that will be reused  
WHERE "oi"."status" = 'Complete'  

Below are ten exploratory → increasingly complex Snowflake SQL snippets (each limited to 20 rows) that build toward the requested analysis. Remember to adapt database / schema / table names exactly as shown.  

